# Jingle Bells, arranged by Claude and SZ. The chorus hook first, then a swung sleigh-ride beat.
title: Jingle Bells
composer: James Lord Pierpont
arranger: Claude & SZ
about: James Lord Pierpont published it in 1857 as One Horse Open Sleigh. It never mentions Christmas. In December 1965 it became the first song played in space: the Gemini 6 astronauts played it on a harmonica and bells they had smuggled aboard.
year: 1857
source: public-domain
category: carols
key: C major
style: chiptune
tempo: 132
time: 4/4

track melody role=lead vol=0.8
